1
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,479
<i>Claire left in a delivery truck?</i>

2
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:14,199
<i>How could you let her leave?</i>

3
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,919
Ms. Cha told the chairman
we couldn't open the vault,

4
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:20,079
<i>so she could replace
Ms. Claire's project with hers.</i>

5
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:21,879
You just won't stop, will you?

6
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:24,359
<i>If you don't want my dad
to switch the project,</i>

7
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:26,039
<i>just bring Claire here now.</i>

8
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:27,640
Can we open the door now?

9
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:31,879
<i>You knew all along that
my aunt is my weakness.</i>

10
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:35,679
<i>All I know is
I have to keep my promise to you.</i>

11
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:37,879
<i>Did you think Ms. Cha would let you live</i>

12
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:39,239
<i>if she found out
you weren't the real Claire?</i>

13
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:40,879
<i>About what you asked.</i>

14
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:43,320
I remember
the pilot drank coffee before boarding.

15
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:56,799
<i>Are you sure I'm nothing more
than a dog, Ms. Cha?</i>

16
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:58,320
You're well aware

17
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:01,080
that I'm more than that.

18
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:13,080
Cha.

19
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:16,200
If you're upset,

20
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:19,880
you can stay at my place.

21
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:23,720
It's okay.

22
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:26,480
I just don't wanna go home
and get scolded by my dad.

23
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:31,000
What about Tunlathon?

24
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:34,560
What about him?

25
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,920
Aren't you gonna do anything?

26
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:42,360
Just go home, Chris. Can I be alone?

27
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:46,440
Go.

28
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,280
Go!

29
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:24,000
Cha!

30
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:31,000
What did you do to her?

31
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,999
I didn't do anything.

32
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,080
I bumped into her.
She lost her balance, so I caught her.

33
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,719
How dare he lay a hand on me?

34
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:45,119
Next time, even if I fall
and break my limbs, it's my business.

35
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:47,040
Don't ever touch me again.

36
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:51,240
If you don't know your place,
I'll have Dad fire you. Got it?

37
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:52,999
Yes, ma'am.

38
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,200
You can go now.

39
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:07,840
He really didn't do anything?

40
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:10,159
Why do you ask?

41
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:11,519
Well,

42
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:13,799
you looked so furious at him.

43
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:15,439
I thought
he must've done something to you.

44
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:17,919
Geez, Mom. It's nothing.

45
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:19,640
I already can't stand him.

46
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:38,320
Don't overthink it. I'm just tired.

47
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:42,400
I have to go. I'll call you later.

48
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:50,400
What is she doing out here at this hour?

49
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:01,400
What are you doing?

50
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,560
Making you pay
for what you did to me earlier.

51
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:18,240
Is that all you've got?

52
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:41,240
Does it hurt?

53
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:45,800
I'm fine.

54
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:50,440
I understand why you had to do it.

55
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:15,040
Where is she?

56
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,200
Cha?

57
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:50,800
Are you in there?

58
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:19,400
Mom. What are you doing here?

59
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:22,760
I followed you.

60
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:25,120
What are you doing in here?

61
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:30,680
Just walking and thinking about work.
I couldn't sleep.

62
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:33,039
What about you?

63
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:36,439
I came to see what you were
sneaking around doing.

64
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:38,119
Sneaking around?

65
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:40,519
I was just walking
and thinking about work.

66
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:41,519
What?

67
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:45,039
You expect me to stay cooped up in my room
and play the maid's daughter?

68
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:47,319
Cha, don't you pick a fight.

69
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:49,320
I'm not. It's true.

70
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:53,320
Anything else?
I'm going to bed. I'm sleepy.

71
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:55,720
DELETE

72
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:08,480
BANGKOK - LADPRAO
MARCH 7TH

73
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:14,200
<i>New customer. Please take their order.</i>

74
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:16,160
Yes, sir.

75
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:32,240
What can I get for you?

76
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:35,160
What do you recommend?

77
00:09:35,760 --> 00:09:37,439
I'll go get you a menu.

78
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:39,440
No need. Just tell me.

79
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:42,399
But the menu has pictures of the dishes.

80
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:44,359
In case you'd like to see them.

81
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:47,800
What the hell!
I just said I didn't want to look.

82
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:49,320
Can't you understand?

83
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:53,560
Is something wrong, ma'am?

84
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:56,759
- Are you the manager?
- Yes.

85
00:09:56,760 --> 00:09:59,480
Did you train your staff
to argue with the customers?

86
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:01,799
I'm very sorry.

87
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:03,920
But don't worry. I'll take your order.

88
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:06,480
Go on. Head to the kitchen.

89
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:17,080
Please have a seat, ma'am.

90
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:25,239
Excuse me, ma'am. Is something wrong?

91
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:28,519
Nothing. I'm just going
to warn everyone online

92
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:31,079
so they don't have
the same awful experience.

93
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:33,600
Hold on, ma'am. Please calm down.

94
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:35,759
I'm truly sorry.

95
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:40,360
If there's anything I can do
to make this right, just let me know.

96
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:43,200
Are you sure?

97
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:45,600
<i>You get it, right?</i>

98
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:48,000
I do.

99
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:51,880
Thank you.

100
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:00,080
Chan.

101
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:04,680
Hey, stop, Chan.

102
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:07,480
Chan.

103
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:11,280
Are you mad at me?

104
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,240
I just don't want you working as a waiter.

105
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:18,360
You don't want me working at all.

106
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:22,920
You show up and cause trouble,
preventing me from working there.

107
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,760
I don't want you working.

108
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:31,440
Chan.

109
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:37,159
What if something happens to me

110
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:39,199
while you're at work?

111
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:40,760
Aren't you worried about me?

112
00:11:44,760 --> 00:11:46,200
You've been fine for a long time.

113
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:50,040
What if it happens again? I don't care.

114
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:52,080
I don't want you working.

115
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:55,160
Your job is to take care of me.

116
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:02,440
Answer me one question.

117
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:04,800
Do you love me?

118
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:11,000
Do you love me?

119
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:18,520
What does "Mm" mean?
Do you love me or not?

120
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:24,359
Are you going to say it?

121
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:27,959
If you don't,
I'll hug and kiss you right here.

122
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:30,520
No, Claire. There are people around.

123
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:32,959
I don't care.

124
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:34,360
You know that.

125
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:37,520
So, do you love me?

126
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:42,240
Of course I do.

127
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:46,039
- Claire.
- You're the best.

128
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:48,359
- People will see.
- So what, Chan?

129
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:50,799
Let me take a picture as proof.

130
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:52,559
So whenever you see it,

131
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:55,479
you'll remember telling me you love me.

132
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:57,080
Smile.

133
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:59,080
Come on, smile.

134
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:01,399
That's enough. It's embarrassing.

135
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:02,839
What's with you?

136
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:04,959
<i>This angle's better.
This side looks nicer.</i>

137
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:06,759
<i>-People are staring.
- See? Much better.</i>

138
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:08,320
<i>Smile.</i>

139
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:19,800
DELETE

140
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:36,760
Hey. I remember now, about what you asked.

141
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,400
What is it?

142
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:42,200
I remember the pilot drank coffee
before boarding.

143
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:45,280
He drank coffee?

144
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,679
<i>The pilot really was drugged.</i>

145
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:53,000
THE BLOOD TEST CONFIRMED
THE PILOT WAS DRUGGED

146
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:04,760
So... what... does it mean?

147
00:14:06,560 --> 00:14:07,600
It's nothing.

148
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:09,800
Let's go.

149
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:40,400
It's late. Aren't you coming to bed?

150
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:43,800
I'm not sleepy. You go ahead.

151
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:46,320
Why is that?

152
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:51,280
Do you really think
Claire kept that secret in the vault?

153
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:54,519
Is that why you wanted
to see it for yourself?

154
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:57,040
You should stop thinking about this.

155
00:14:58,240 --> 00:15:00,879
The proof Claire claimed
she had doesn't exist.

156
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:02,600
Do you know why?

157
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:05,600
Because I never did that.

158
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:13,840
If I was going to cheat on you,

159
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:17,640
I would've done it back
when you were sick.

160
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:22,800
Why would I think that?

161
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:30,400
This move might be better.

162
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:36,440
Mr. Thiwa.

163
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:39,560
Were you even listening to me?

164
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:44,399
Did you know?

165
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:49,080
They say playing Go trains you
to read people's minds.

166
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:53,359
Because every move

167
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:56,600
reveals what the player wants.

168
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:00,239
Just like a lot of people.

169
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:04,999
Everything they do is
for the one thing they want.

170
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:09,399
Can you stop focusing on
this stupid game and hear me out?

171
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:13,079
Why would anyone do anything
if they get nothing in return?

172
00:16:13,080 --> 00:16:15,239
I know. I understand. I heard you say

173
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:17,800
you never cheated on me. That you love me.

174
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:20,479
Then let me ask you this.

175
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:23,760
If I wasn't leaving anything
to you or your daughter,

176
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:26,080
would you still love me?

177
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:48,040
Let's talk about this later.

178
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:50,760
I'm going upstairs.

179
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:53,840
Don't be long.

180
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,000
Please look after him.

181
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:20,599
I hope you didn't stay up for us.

182
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,519
No.

183
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:25,720
I had a lot on my mind today,

184
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:30,280
so I decided to play Go to clear my head.

185
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:36,320
Do you like playing Go?

186
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:41,800
You know I always play it
whenever I need to think.

187
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:45,800
Play a game with me.

188
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:49,760
I don't know how.

189
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:54,560
Uh, I mean I don't remember
how to play this game.

190
00:17:55,120 --> 00:17:57,040
Come on, play a game with me.

191
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:01,920
- Uh...
- Sir,

192
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:04,120
I don't think she...

193
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:06,839
You should try it.

194
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:08,879
You used to beat me at this.

195
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:13,000
Even if you've forgotten,
I'm sure some of it is still with you.

196
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:15,120
Come on, just one game.

197
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:20,640
What would you do?

198
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:25,880
How about this?

199
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,240
I would do this.

200
00:19:03,840 --> 00:19:07,479
If we don't separate black and white,
and put them all together,

201
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,960
then we've claimed the whole board, right?

202
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:18,240
Oh, you're right.

203
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:20,719
Now that's thinking outside the box.

204
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:22,320
Why didn't I think of that?

205
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:25,639
Come on, Grandpa.

206
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:28,199
The game's over. It's time for bed.

207
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:30,240
You've had a long day.

208
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:39,680
Fine, I'll go to bed.

209
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:42,959
I look forward

210
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:46,320
to seeing what you two came up with
for the 60th anniversary event.

211
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:48,000
Okay.

212
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:09,560
I didn't expect you to mess up his board.

213
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:12,640
I don't think he expected it either.

214
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:16,120
Wanna know the truth?

215
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:17,840
What truth?

216
00:20:19,560 --> 00:20:21,999
I didn't want him
doing anything stressful.

217
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:25,240
Today was stressful enough.
Then he played a stressful game.

218
00:20:26,280 --> 00:20:28,479
I was worried it would affect his heart.

219
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:31,440
So I just messed up the board. How's that?

220
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:37,240
Thank you.

221
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:40,960
Huh? Wait...

222
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:43,919
Am I hearing things?

223
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:45,600
Did you just thank me?

224
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,680
What's that for, huh?

225
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:55,240
Well...

226
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:59,159
For looking out for him,

227
00:20:59,160 --> 00:21:01,760
even though
he's not your real grandfather.

228
00:21:05,360 --> 00:21:06,639
I don't know.

229
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:09,520
Maybe I've grown attached to him.

230
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:14,319
We're helping each other.

231
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:17,680
You take care of my aunt,
and I take care of him.

232
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:28,480
You know, you and him
are actually a lot alike.

233
00:21:29,800 --> 00:21:30,960
How?

234
00:21:32,880 --> 00:21:34,560
You're both awful at smiling.

235
00:21:39,280 --> 00:21:40,920
See? There it is.

236
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,960
Oh, you're acting cool. Give me a smile.

237
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:48,760
Smile.

238
00:21:55,320 --> 00:21:56,480
Stop acting cool.

239
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:06,720
I need to take this call.

240
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:09,480
Can you go to your room on your own?

241
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:13,480
Wait.

242
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:20,279
About what I asked you
regarding the pilot today...

243
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:22,000
don't tell anyone.

244
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:24,400
Who would I tell?

245
00:22:25,080 --> 00:22:26,880
You don't let me talk to anyone.

246
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,280
Just making sure you know.

247
00:22:30,320 --> 00:22:31,680
I know now.

248
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:34,800
I'm going.

249
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:44,680
Hello?

250
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:49,439
Were you able to recover
the data from Claire's phone?

251
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:50,560
<i>Yes.</i>

252
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:08,080
Did I forget to close the door?

253
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:14,800
What?

254
00:23:46,840 --> 00:23:48,760
- Ms. Claire!
- He killed me.

255
00:23:49,720 --> 00:23:51,919
- Ms. Claire!
- He killed me! He killed me!

256
00:23:51,920 --> 00:23:53,479
- I said he killed me.
- Ms. Claire.

257
00:23:53,480 --> 00:23:54,759
- Ms. Claire.
- Can you hear me?

258
00:23:54,760 --> 00:23:58,359
He killed me. He killed me. He killed me.

259
00:23:58,360 --> 00:23:59,960
I said he killed me.

260
00:24:01,200 --> 00:24:02,520
Can you hear me?

261
00:24:15,560 --> 00:24:17,320
Mr. Chan, it's all your fault.

262
00:24:18,040 --> 00:24:21,720
I was finally starting to forget.
Now I'm dreaming about her.

263
00:24:33,080 --> 00:24:35,719
<i>Ms. Claire, you said...</i>

264
00:24:35,720 --> 00:24:39,880
you'd have nothing to live for
once your grandfather was gone.

265
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:44,279
- But what about Mr. Chan, your fiancé?
- What about him?

266
00:24:44,280 --> 00:24:47,479
People who are engaged
are supposed to love each other.

267
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:49,759
Aren't you worried...

268
00:24:49,760 --> 00:24:52,480
he would be sad
if something happened to you?

269
00:24:53,120 --> 00:24:54,040
Sad?

270
00:24:54,920 --> 00:24:58,840
<i>I think he'd be the happiest one
if I died.</i>

271
00:25:00,480 --> 00:25:01,960
Does that mean...

272
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:04,720
he wanted Ms. Claire dead?

273
00:25:32,360 --> 00:25:33,440
Cha.

274
00:25:34,600 --> 00:25:36,040
How are you feeling, dear?

275
00:25:37,400 --> 00:25:40,520
Are you excited
for your first day at work?

276
00:25:41,520 --> 00:25:44,159
Thank you for trusting me
with a job at TGL.

277
00:25:44,160 --> 00:25:45,640
Listen to you.

278
00:25:46,160 --> 00:25:48,320
Of course your dad trusts you.

279
00:25:48,840 --> 00:25:52,959
But that's because he sees your talent.

280
00:25:52,960 --> 00:25:57,760
Otherwise, why would he let you
work at the company he loves?

281
00:25:59,240 --> 00:26:00,400
Right, honey?

282
00:26:02,280 --> 00:26:03,999
Don't let your mom and me down.

283
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:05,200
I won't.

284
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:08,040
Why didn't you run it by me, Grandpa?

285
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:15,920
Come on.

286
00:26:16,440 --> 00:26:19,199
It's just hiring a new employee.

287
00:26:19,200 --> 00:26:21,120
Why would he need permission?

288
00:26:21,720 --> 00:26:22,959
Besides...

289
00:26:22,960 --> 00:26:25,919
I've never seen...

290
00:26:25,920 --> 00:26:31,320
a chairman ask the vice chairman
for permission to hire someone.

291
00:26:32,400 --> 00:26:36,320
That would be absolutely ridiculous.

292
00:26:38,280 --> 00:26:39,320
Really?

293
00:26:39,960 --> 00:26:43,280
Well, I've never seen a maid
give unsolicited advice like you do.

294
00:26:45,920 --> 00:26:46,759
Grandpa.

295
00:26:46,760 --> 00:26:49,719
If you want her to work,
send her somewhere else.

296
00:26:49,720 --> 00:26:52,160
We have plenty of companies. Why TGL?

297
00:26:53,560 --> 00:26:55,960
I don't want to work
with a maid's daughter.

298
00:26:57,200 --> 00:27:00,960
Why not? Afraid she'll outshine you?

299
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:04,560
Cha. Don't, dear.

300
00:27:05,440 --> 00:27:06,880
What did you just say?

301
00:27:08,680 --> 00:27:10,519
I'm telling the truth, Mom.

302
00:27:10,520 --> 00:27:12,719
This maid's daughter

303
00:27:12,720 --> 00:27:15,240
may end up contributing
more to the company than someone...

304
00:27:15,920 --> 00:27:18,119
who does nothing but cause trouble...

305
00:27:18,120 --> 00:27:21,360
just because
she's the chairman's granddaughter.

306
00:27:24,320 --> 00:27:25,760
- Watch your mouth.
- Cha!

307
00:27:26,640 --> 00:27:27,759
- Cha!
- Claire!

308
00:27:27,760 --> 00:27:29,199
- Big mouth, aren't you?
- Claire!

309
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:30,479
- Big mouth, aren't you?
- Claire, stop!

310
00:27:30,480 --> 00:27:32,599
- Claire!
- Ms. Claire!

311
00:27:32,600 --> 00:27:33,839
- Mr. Thiwa!
- Ms. Claire!

312
00:27:33,840 --> 00:27:36,159
- Honey?
- Please stop, Ms. Claire. Please stop.

313
00:27:36,160 --> 00:27:37,920
You dare stop me?

314
00:27:39,720 --> 00:27:41,600
Please don't upset the chairman.

315
00:27:44,680 --> 00:27:46,000
Please stop, Claire.

316
00:27:51,240 --> 00:27:52,440
You want me to stop?

317
00:27:54,120 --> 00:27:55,160
Fine.

318
00:27:58,840 --> 00:28:00,839
- Claire!
- Who do you think you are?

319
00:28:00,840 --> 00:28:04,960
A guard dog doesn't get to bark
at its master. Got it?

320
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:08,920
Yes.

321
00:28:10,760 --> 00:28:11,920
Look at me.

322
00:28:15,840 --> 00:28:17,120
Claire!

323
00:28:27,800 --> 00:28:29,040
Claire, stop!

324
00:28:31,640 --> 00:28:35,040
Stop it, Claire! I said stop right now!

325
00:29:24,840 --> 00:29:26,760
- Ms. Cha?
- I brought your medicine.

326
00:29:30,800 --> 00:29:31,879
You should go.

327
00:29:31,880 --> 00:29:34,959
If Ms. Claire sees you,
you'll be in trouble again.

328
00:29:34,960 --> 00:29:38,000
What? You think I can't handle myself?

329
00:29:38,680 --> 00:29:40,680
I'd like to see
what else that bitch can do.

330
00:29:41,600 --> 00:29:42,480
Besides...

331
00:29:43,880 --> 00:29:45,879
you're her bodyguard.

332
00:29:45,880 --> 00:29:47,919
You helped me back there.

333
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:49,960
She'll think you're taking my side.

334
00:29:51,160 --> 00:29:52,240
Why did you do it?

335
00:30:08,680 --> 00:30:09,880
Maybe because...

336
00:30:11,920 --> 00:30:13,240
I can't stand...

337
00:30:14,560 --> 00:30:16,800
seeing her hurt you.

338
00:31:20,880 --> 00:31:23,600
Cha. Come here.

339
00:31:26,480 --> 00:31:27,799
What now, Mom?

340
00:31:27,800 --> 00:31:30,880
I think we should
get rid of Claire quickly.

341
00:31:31,480 --> 00:31:34,880
I don't care how--
Kill her, cripple her, make her disappear.

342
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:37,400
What's going on? What are you up to?

343
00:31:38,680 --> 00:31:42,440
Last night, Mr. Thiwa implied
he was leaving everything to Claire.

344
00:31:43,680 --> 00:31:46,160
- Huh?
- I don't know...

345
00:31:46,760 --> 00:31:48,360
if he was testing me.

346
00:31:49,920 --> 00:31:52,040
But I'm not taking even a 1% chance.

347
00:31:53,200 --> 00:31:54,599
You're well aware

348
00:31:54,600 --> 00:31:56,919
if Claire becomes the chairman,

349
00:31:56,920 --> 00:31:58,920
she won't keep us around.

350
00:32:16,640 --> 00:32:18,239
Where's Mr. Chan today?

351
00:32:18,240 --> 00:32:20,159
He's not here to boss me around.

352
00:32:20,160 --> 00:32:22,160
He had an urgent matter.

353
00:32:23,040 --> 00:32:25,319
Did you need to talk to him?

354
00:32:25,320 --> 00:32:26,719
No.

355
00:32:26,720 --> 00:32:28,600
I actually wanted to talk to you.

356
00:32:30,560 --> 00:32:31,720
About what?

357
00:32:35,720 --> 00:32:36,719
Well,

358
00:32:36,720 --> 00:32:40,519
he asked me yesterday
if the helicopter pilot

359
00:32:40,520 --> 00:32:43,320
ate or drank anything before takeoff.

360
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:45,920
I was wondering why he wanted to know.

361
00:32:48,440 --> 00:32:50,839
Why didn't you just ask him?

362
00:32:50,840 --> 00:32:56,240
Well, he was just curious,
so I didn't want to pry.

363
00:33:00,160 --> 00:33:04,880
Hey. Do you know anything
about Ms. Claire and Mr. Chan?

364
00:33:06,120 --> 00:33:08,159
I was wondering if they had a fight,

365
00:33:08,160 --> 00:33:11,040
or if there was something more serious.

366
00:33:14,920 --> 00:33:16,480
Are you saying...

367
00:33:18,480 --> 00:33:20,959
you think Mr. Chan
was involved in the crash?

368
00:33:20,960 --> 00:33:24,520
Whoa, no. That's not what I mean at all.

369
00:33:26,520 --> 00:33:27,679
I don't know.

370
00:33:27,680 --> 00:33:31,159
He didn't seem that upset,
so I started wondering.

371
00:33:31,160 --> 00:33:32,800
Anyway, forget it. Ignore me.

372
00:33:33,600 --> 00:33:35,200
He's always been like that.

373
00:33:38,440 --> 00:33:39,600
Who knows?

374
00:33:40,800 --> 00:33:43,080
He might be the one hurting the most.

375
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:47,679
He's unavailable today.

376
00:33:47,680 --> 00:33:50,400
If you need anything, just let me know.

377
00:33:53,280 --> 00:33:54,360
Hold on.

378
00:33:59,800 --> 00:34:02,239
There's somewhere I'd like to go.

379
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:03,800
Could you take me there?

380
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:21,239
Why this temple?

381
00:34:23,199 --> 00:34:25,280
I used to come here with my aunt.

382
00:34:26,679 --> 00:34:28,120
It's so peaceful here.

383
00:34:36,440 --> 00:34:39,639
Actually, I came to
make merit for Ms. Claire.

384
00:34:44,719 --> 00:34:46,120
I dreamed about her last night.

385
00:34:47,360 --> 00:34:50,120
Besides, ever since the crash...

386
00:34:51,080 --> 00:34:53,760
and I've had to become her.

387
00:34:54,520 --> 00:34:56,439
I have no idea how she feels.

388
00:34:56,440 --> 00:34:58,560
So I wanted to let her know.

389
00:35:00,920 --> 00:35:03,520
Then go ahead. I'll wait in the van.

390
00:35:24,480 --> 00:35:28,240
Write the name of the deceased
and bring it to me.

391
00:35:31,640 --> 00:35:35,400
Who was the deceased to you?

392
00:35:39,640 --> 00:35:40,800
A friend, sir.

393
00:35:45,760 --> 00:35:46,760
KHAEDARUN KANCHATHARA

394
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:09,240
- Wan?
- You?

395
00:36:17,400 --> 00:36:19,800
KHAEDARUN KANCHATHARA

396
00:36:26,040 --> 00:36:26,920
Thank you.

397
00:36:38,920 --> 00:36:42,240
And what about you? Why are you here?

398
00:36:42,920 --> 00:36:44,880
To make merit for my late friend.

399
00:36:45,800 --> 00:36:46,760
Perfect.

400
00:36:47,360 --> 00:36:51,600
She's making merit
for her late friend as well.

401
00:36:52,440 --> 00:36:57,439
Please write your late friend's name
on the paper.

402
00:36:57,440 --> 00:36:59,520
Then bring it to me.

403
00:37:00,560 --> 00:37:01,600
Here.

404
00:37:18,720 --> 00:37:20,480
JINLA PHIANDAIDEE

405
00:37:26,720 --> 00:37:31,000
Next, prepare to make the offering, okay?

406
00:37:52,160 --> 00:37:53,840
JINLA PHIANDAIDEE

407
00:38:00,720 --> 00:38:03,400
KHAEDARUN KANCHATHARA

408
00:38:10,200 --> 00:38:13,280
JINLA PHIANDAIDEE

409
00:38:30,280 --> 00:38:31,320
Ms. Wan.

410
00:38:32,960 --> 00:38:34,040
Ms. Wan.

411
00:38:35,040 --> 00:38:37,200
I didn't expect to run into you here.

412
00:38:45,600 --> 00:38:47,040
Neither did I.

413
00:38:47,880 --> 00:38:50,000
Did you make merit for Ms. Jinla?

414
00:38:50,520 --> 00:38:54,759
The last time we met, I could see
how devastated you were over her.

415
00:38:54,760 --> 00:38:57,200
So I figured you came here for her.

416
00:39:00,600 --> 00:39:01,560
Ms. Wan.

417
00:39:02,520 --> 00:39:04,119
If you have a moment, I...

418
00:39:04,120 --> 00:39:06,360
Could you please leave me alone?

419
00:39:08,120 --> 00:39:10,159
I got fired.

420
00:39:10,160 --> 00:39:11,720
Happy now?

421
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:13,679
What?

422
00:39:13,680 --> 00:39:15,679
Don't pretend to be nice.

423
00:39:15,680 --> 00:39:17,320
I know what you're like.

424
00:39:18,120 --> 00:39:20,519
You were mad about
what I did to you that day.

425
00:39:20,520 --> 00:39:23,360
So you pressured my company
to fire me, didn't you?

426
00:39:25,160 --> 00:39:27,039
What else do you want to do to me?

427
00:39:27,040 --> 00:39:28,959
Hurt me?

428
00:39:28,960 --> 00:39:30,239
Slap me?

429
00:39:30,240 --> 00:39:31,520
Go ahead.

430
00:39:33,040 --> 00:39:34,960
I'm standing right here.

431
00:39:57,720 --> 00:39:59,600
She thinks I killed Claire?

432
00:40:00,720 --> 00:40:03,200
<i>I don't know what Ms. Claire told her.</i>

433
00:40:03,960 --> 00:40:07,080
After you asked about the pilot,
she started getting suspicious.

434
00:40:07,760 --> 00:40:10,880
<i>I think it's time you tell her the truth.</i>

435
00:40:11,720 --> 00:40:13,400
Maybe it's better this way.

436
00:40:14,440 --> 00:40:15,920
So she'll stay alert.

437
00:40:17,640 --> 00:40:19,039
You should too.

438
00:40:19,040 --> 00:40:23,400
From what I found out, that pilot
was filling in for our regular pilot.

439
00:40:24,240 --> 00:40:25,360
What are you saying?

440
00:40:27,040 --> 00:40:30,040
Hey, Chan. I have to go. Talk later.

441
00:40:41,640 --> 00:40:42,680
How was it?

442
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:45,720
Did it make you feel better?

443
00:40:46,880 --> 00:40:49,360
Did you guys pressure
<i>The Contenic</i> to fire Wan?

444
00:40:49,960 --> 00:40:50,920
What?

445
00:40:51,720 --> 00:40:52,960
I just ran into Wan.

446
00:40:53,760 --> 00:40:55,400
She came to make merit for me.

447
00:40:57,360 --> 00:40:58,400
Wan...

448
00:40:59,600 --> 00:41:01,839
Oh, you mean Wanwali, your friend?

449
00:41:01,840 --> 00:41:03,120
Yes.

450
00:41:03,640 --> 00:41:06,320
Her company fired her.
Was that Mr. Chan's doing?

451
00:41:09,200 --> 00:41:10,719
I don't think he'd do that.

452
00:41:10,720 --> 00:41:14,799
I think her company fired her
as punishment

453
00:41:14,800 --> 00:41:17,200
and to take responsibility.

454
00:41:18,880 --> 00:41:21,440
I know what she did was extreme.

455
00:41:22,000 --> 00:41:25,240
But she did it
because she was upset about me.

456
00:41:26,880 --> 00:41:29,479
Ms. Wan came all that way to attack you.

457
00:41:29,480 --> 00:41:34,119
Don't forget, you're a celebrity
and the vice chairman of TGL.

458
00:41:34,120 --> 00:41:36,880
Did you expect her company to do nothing?

459
00:41:42,640 --> 00:41:44,079
Let's just go.

460
00:41:44,080 --> 00:41:47,000
I don't think Chan would like me
bringing you here.

461
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:08,560
Here, Mr. Chan.

462
00:42:12,760 --> 00:42:15,240
I'm sorry we couldn't repair it.

463
00:42:16,760 --> 00:42:18,240
But it's not a problem.

464
00:42:24,240 --> 00:42:26,840
I was able to recover the data
for the new phone.

465
00:42:29,120 --> 00:42:33,759
I saved all of Ms. Claire's data on it.

466
00:42:33,760 --> 00:42:35,719
And I cloned the SIM card for you.

467
00:42:35,720 --> 00:42:38,200
You can just pop it into the new phone.

468
00:42:39,160 --> 00:42:41,360
If that's all, I'll take my leave.

469
00:43:10,560 --> 00:43:11,399
SATURDAY 9 MARCH

470
00:43:11,400 --> 00:43:14,040
MOBILE

471
00:43:26,680 --> 00:43:29,600
SLIDE TO ANSWER

472
00:43:41,240 --> 00:43:43,000
What if we hired Wan?

473
00:43:45,440 --> 00:43:46,400
What do you mean?

474
00:43:47,080 --> 00:43:51,040
She lost her job because of me,
so I want to help her out.

475
00:43:51,920 --> 00:43:53,279
I don't think it will work.

476
00:43:53,280 --> 00:43:55,919
I know you want to help your friend.

477
00:43:55,920 --> 00:43:58,360
But Chan wouldn't allow it.

478
00:43:59,000 --> 00:44:02,880
This is about your safety
and your secrets.

479
00:44:04,320 --> 00:44:06,720
But just this once.
Would he really say no?

480
00:44:08,800 --> 00:44:11,960
I'm Ms. Claire, Vice Chairman of TGL.

481
00:44:13,240 --> 00:44:15,039
On the outside, yes.

482
00:44:15,040 --> 00:44:18,280
But no matter what,
you're not the real Ms. Claire.

483
00:44:31,240 --> 00:44:32,640
Take me to the office.

484
00:44:45,680 --> 00:44:47,679
<i>I've just realized something.</i>

485
00:44:47,680 --> 00:44:52,240
<i>No matter how hard I try,
I can never become the real Ms. Claire.</i>

486
00:44:53,480 --> 00:44:55,400
<i>So why must I be exactly like her?</i>

487
00:45:23,960 --> 00:45:25,000
<i>Yes, Ms. Claire?</i>

488
00:45:25,880 --> 00:45:29,359
Call a meeting with every department
involved in the 60th anniversary event.

489
00:45:29,360 --> 00:45:30,760
<i>Yes, Ms. Claire.</i>

490
00:45:45,040 --> 00:45:45,959
TYCOON WITH A HEART OF GOLD,

491
00:45:45,960 --> 00:45:47,080
DONATES 120 MILLION FOR MEDICAL EQUIPMENT,
A MODERN-DAY SAINT

492
00:45:52,360 --> 00:45:53,640
<i>From now on,</i>

493
00:45:54,760 --> 00:45:56,720
<i>I'm gonna be Claire in my own way.</i>

494
00:46:25,480 --> 00:46:26,999
<i>You called a team meeting?</i>

495
00:46:27,000 --> 00:46:28,479
Have you lost your mind?

496
00:46:28,480 --> 00:46:31,320
<i>Ms. Claire wants you to work for us.</i>

497
00:46:31,920 --> 00:46:34,479
<i>I bet Ms. Claire's faking amnesia.</i>

498
00:46:34,480 --> 00:46:36,479
<i>Or she wouldn't go on Wonder's show.</i>

499
00:46:36,480 --> 00:46:39,999
<i>By now everyone knows
Claire's out of the hospital.</i>

500
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:42,239
<i>They'll look for another chance to strike.</i>

501
00:46:42,240 --> 00:46:46,080
<i>Please welcome Ms. Cha
with a round of applause!</i>

502
00:46:46,880 --> 00:46:48,799
- Whoa, sir!
- Who sent you?

503
00:46:48,800 --> 00:46:51,359
- No one, sir! Ow!
- Who sent you?

504
00:46:51,360 --> 00:46:55,159
<i>Would you like to kneel at my feet
and apologize to me?</i>

505
00:46:55,160 --> 00:46:58,280
MS. KHAEDARUN OPENS UP
AFTER SURVIVING A NEAR-DEATH EXPERIENCE
